šÍi<?php exit; ?>a:2:{s:7:"content";O:8:"stdClass":24:{s:2:"ID";i:5362;s:11:"post_author";s:1:"1";s:9:"post_date";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:02";s:13:"post_date_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:02";s:12:"post_content";s:979:"<h3 class="blog-details__h3">Working agreements that stuck</h3><figure class="blog-details__figure wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nsc.test/wp-content/themes/NSC-Software/frontend/build/img/blog8.webp" alt="Incident Response Playbooks That Work â€” delivery context" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" /></figure><p>NSC templates include customer comms drafts and legal checkpoints so tired humans do not improvise under pressure.</p><h2 class="blog-details__h2">What we are seeing in practice</h2><p>Playbooks nobody rehearses are fantasy novels. Incident response improves when you simulate partial failures and rotate commanders.</p><p>If you are planning a similar initiative, start with a thin end-to-end slice, instrument it in production, and expand scope only when telemetry supports the next bet.</p><h2 class="blog-details__h2">Summary</h2><p>Blameless postmortems require psychological safety and executives who show up without firing questions.</p>";s:10:"post_title";s:37:"Incident Response Playbooks That Work";s:12:"post_excerpt";s:277:"Incident Response Playbooks That Work â€” Playbooks nobody rehearses are fantasy novels. Incident response improves when you simulate partial failures and rotate commanders. Blameless postmortems require psychological safety and executives who show up without firing questions.";s:11:"post_status";s:7:"publish";s:14:"comment_status";s:4:"open";s:11:"ping_status";s:4:"open";s:13:"post_password";s:0:"";s:9:"post_name";s:37:"incident-response-playbooks-that-work";s:7:"to_ping";s:0:"";s:6:"pinged";s:0:"";s:13:"post_modified";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:02";s:17:"post_modified_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:02";s:21:"post_content_filtered";s:0:"";s:11:"post_parent";i:0;s:4:"guid";s:55:"https://nsc.test/incident-respo